# Frontend Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values.

# ── Required in production ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# URL of the Express backend API server (no trailing slash).
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the client bundle at BUILD time. If this
# is missing in production, `next build` fails on purpose: the previous behaviour
# fell back to http://localhost:4000, so every visitor's browser would post their
# enquiry to their own machine and the lead would be lost with no server-side
# trace anywhere.
#
# This value is public by definition (it ships to the browser). Never put a
# secret here, and never treat it as authentication — the backend enforces its
# own CORS policy and rate limits.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# ── Optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google Analytics 4 Measurement ID.
#
# Setting this ENABLES the consent banner rather than turning tracking on: the GA
# tag is not loaded at all until the visitor accepts. If it is unset, no banner is
# shown and nothing is tracked.
#
# How it works:
#   - Every page load tells Google Consent Mode v2 that analytics_storage is DENIED.
#   - The visitor gets an "Accept analytics" / "Decline" choice, stored in
#     localStorage. Declining is as prominent as accepting; a choice extracted by
#     making refusal harder is not freely given.
#   - Only after accepting is the tag loaded. Before any choice, nothing is sent.
#   - Bumping the consent version invalidates previous choices so they are asked
#     for again, rather than being assumed to cover a changed policy.
#   - IP anonymisation is on and cookies are marked SameSite=Lax; Secure. Neither
#     makes tracking acceptable without consent — they reduce what is collected
#     from someone who has given it.
#
# Google's own guidance is that Consent Mode is not a substitute for consent, and
# that a tag must not fire before the choice is made. This follows that.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=

# Canonical site URL used in metadata / OpenGraph / sitemap / robots.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://larptech.io
